  "question": "A £60 price tag includes 20% VAT. How many pounds of it is VAT?",
  "value": 10,
  "unit": "pounds",
  "answer": "VAT = 60 - 50 = 10 pounds.",
  "move": "Ask which number the percentage was taken from.",
  "trap": "Taking 20% of £60, which is £12.",
  "hint": "The 20% was added to the price before tax, not to the £60.",
  "steps": [
    "The pre-tax price plus 20% makes 60, so 1.2 x price = 60.",
    "Pre-tax price = 60 / 1.2 = 50.",
    "VAT = 60 - 50 = 10 pounds."
